        "هِ قَوْلٌ مَعْلُومٌ فَقَالَ «أَثْنِ عَلَى رَبِّكَ وَ صَلِّ عَلَى نَبِيِّكَ وَ اِسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْبِكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.933 - Al-Halabi asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about what should be said in the Qunoot (the supplication during prayer).\nImam (as) replied: \"Praise your Lord (azj), send blessings upon your Prophet, and seek forgiveness for your sins.\""
        ]
      }
